---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/therapy-scheduling-software/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="ed-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">Mental health EHR</a>{" "}
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">
          Therapy Scheduling Software for Independent Practices
        </span>
      </nav>
      <div class="ed-feature-hero">
        <section class="ed-hero">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Scheduling for mental health practices</div>
            <h1>
              Make space for care.
              <br />
              <em>And the day around it.</em>
            </h1>
            <p class="ed-dek">
              Plan your recurring week, adjust appointments, and keep patient
              context close. Otto connects the calendar with the work of
              preparing for and completing each visit.
            </p>
            <div class="ed-actions">
              <a class="button" href="/waitlist/">
                Join the waitlist ↗
              </a>
              <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
                Watch the 2-minute demo ↗
              </a>
            </div>
            <p class="micro">
              For independent mental health practices · Built by Tebra
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ed-hero-art">
            <div class="art">
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 640 500"
                preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <rect width="640" height="500" fill="#e0d3c8" />
                <circle cx="122" cy="116" r="160" fill="#f0eee8" />
                <path d="M0 385 640 275v225H0z" fill="#cbdde0" />
                <g transform="translate(167 96) rotate(6 150 150)">
                  <rect
                    x="13"
                    y="14"
                    width="310"
                    height="285"
                    rx="15"
                    fill="#004852"
                    opacity=".12"
                  />
                  <rect width="310" height="285" rx="15" fill="#f6f3eb" />
                  <path
                    d="M0 15a15 15 0 0 1 15-15h280a15 15 0 0 1 15 15v61H0z"
                    fill="#004852"
                  />
                  <path
                    d="M73-17v40m164-40v40"
                    stroke="#8ca7a2"
                    stroke-width="13"
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                  />
                  <g fill="#cbdde0">
                    <rect x="30" y="102" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="99" y="102" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="169" y="102" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="239" y="102" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="30" y="159" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="99" y="159" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="239" y="159" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="30" y="216" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="99" y="216" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="169" y="216" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                    <rect x="239" y="216" width="41" height="34" rx="5" />
                  </g>
                  <rect
                    x="169"
                    y="159"
                    width="41"
                    height="34"
                    rx="5"
                    fill="#b85c38"
                  />
                  <path
                    d="m178 175 8 8 13-17"
                    fill="none"
                    stroke="#fff"
                    stroke-width="3"
                  />
                </g>
                <path
                  d="m490 380 30-150"
                  stroke="#b85c38"
                  stroke-width="15"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                />
                <path d="m490 380-5 26 14-23" fill="#004852" />
              </svg>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">The work, connected</span>
            <h2>A calendar connected to what comes next.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            The appointment is the starting point. Let it lead you into the
            patient context and the next step in the visit.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>See the week clearly</h3>
            <p>
              Use week and agenda views to orient yourself, with a mobile
              schedule for a smaller screen.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>Keep recurring care organized</h3>
            <p>
              Create recurring appointments, edit or reschedule visits, and
              block time away from the practice.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Prepare from the appointment</h3>
            <p>
              Move from the schedule into patient information and visit
              preparation before the conversation begins.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-story">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Inside the workflow</span>
          <h2>Plan a week that reflects how you work.</h2>
          <p>
            Recurring sessions give a practice its rhythm. Time-off blocks and
            conflict checking help you protect space around that rhythm as
            appointments change.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
            See the complete visit ↗
          </a>
        </div>
        <ul class="ed-checks">
          <li>Week, agenda, and mobile views</li>
          <li>Recurring appointments and rescheduling</li>
          <li>Time-off blocks and conflict checking</li>
          <li>Patient context connected to the visit</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-faq">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</span>
          <h2>Get to know the details.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Can I schedule recurring sessions?</summary>
            <p>
              Otto’s public feature list includes recurring appointments as well
              as editing and rescheduling.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I block time away?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. Otto lists time-off blocks and conflict checking among its
              scheduling features.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>
              Does this include patient self-booking and reminders?
            </summary>
            <p>
              Confirm the current self-booking, reminder, and communication
              options for your account. This page does not promise those
              capabilities.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I manage a multi-provider practice?</summary>
            <p>
              Tell the team about provider seats, access levels, supervision,
              and shared scheduling needs so they can confirm current fit.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</span>
        <div class="ed-resources">
          <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">The mental health EHR ↗</a>
          <a href="/ai-progress-notes/">AI progress notes ↗</a>
          <a href="/compare/">Compare your options ↗</a>
          <a href="/tools/">Free practice tools ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-close">
        <div>
          <h2>See what a connected practice day can feel like.</h2>
          <p>
            Watch Otto carry a visit from preparation through documentation and
            payment. Then tell us about the way you practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </section>
      <p class="ed-source">
        Product details checked against{" "}
        <a href="https://otto.tebra.com/">Otto’s public website</a> on October
        16, 2026. Confirm availability and service terms for your practice.
        Workflow examples are illustrative and use fictional information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
